, 111, 101, 81, 71, 118, 116, 114, 133) \u2014 no discontinuity marking a candidate change point.\n\n**The key finding: the partner set never changes.** Individual members activate in a staggered, baton-passing sequence (steps 10\u201321): node 59 owns [56322,61322], 325\u2192610 in [61322,66322], 617/642 in [66322,71322], 826 in [71322,76322], 881/991 in [76322,81322], 1034/1641 in [81322,86322]. Each member is a ~90-event burst then goes silent.\n\nBut when I resolve *who* each active member talks to, the answer is the same core set every time:\n\n- node 59, early [56322,61322] (step_22): {58, 138, 247, 383, 393, 402, 424, 429, 613, 686, 721, 794, 861, 879, 895, 928, 944, 959, 970, 1014, 1032, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1291, 1605, 1713, 1757, 1761, 1999} + 1443\n- node 1641, late [81322,86322] (step_28): the identical 30-node set\n\nMid-period members (83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 826, 881, 991, 1034 \u2014 steps 23\u201327, 29\u201331) all reproduce this same set, with only idiosyncratic singletons (1443, 1478, 1681, 1512, 807, 1185). Jaccard(before, after) \u2248 0.93 (step_32).\n\n**Confounder control.** The apparent \"turnover\" is turnover of *which group node is active*, not of contacts \u2014 the classic false positive for regime-switch detection. Node 881's near-zero activity outside [76322,81322] (steps 04\u201307, 09) confirms the staggered-activation artifact rather than a partner migration.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8155967f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [59, 83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 743, 826, 881, 991, 1034, 1641],\n  \"window\": [56322, 86322],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No abrupt change of interaction partners. The group's contacts are drawn from a fixed ~30-node core set (58,138,247,383,393,402,424,429,613,686,721,794,861,879,895,928,944,959,970,1014,1032,1071,1136,1283,1291,1605,1713,1757,1761,1999) at every point in [56322,86322]; Jaccard between the earliest and latest 5000-unit half-windows is ~0.93. What varies is which group member is emitting: members fire in a staggered relay of ~90-event bursts, each silent outside its slot. That per-node activation schedule mimics turnover but leaves the partner set invariant, so there is neither an old-set/new-set handover nor gradual drift \u2014 the correct reading is a stable regime with rotating emitters. Total volume is likewise flat across the period, ruling out a volume-driven change point.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 56810, "total_output_tokens": 7406, "total_tokens": 64216, "total_latency_ms": 98191, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}